# Floppy controller ROM 253, 160000-167777: an earlier version of the disk
# driver and boot loader, which bk doesn't use.
#
# From gid's commented IDA disassembly of this ROM, 253_koi8.zip from
# https://gid.pdp-11.net/sources.html; its input's MD5 is this ROM's, and
# all 601 of its instructions are here at the addresses it gives. Its names
# and its routine descriptions, translated.
#
# Cell 52, GRAFST in bk0010.ann (the monitor's graphics erase flag),
# holds this driver's error code (ERRFDD in the source).

code 160016 BOOT0
head 160016 Automatic boot: try drive 0, then the next ones; with no loader
head 160016 anywhere, STOP.

code 160062 BOOT1
head 160062 Boot from the drive given in R0.

code 160072 STOP
head 160072 Stop the floppy motor and leave.

code 160120 BOOT
head 160120 Read block 0 (400 words) to 1000 and start it, if it begins with NOP
head 160120 (240) and its second instruction isn't RESET (a non-system disk).

code 160216 RWSEC
head 160216 Read or write by track and sector.

code 160220 INIT
head 160220 Initialize the driver's work area (R3): track table, head and step
head 160220 delays, precompensation track, retries, 10 sectors a track.

code 160304 RWBLK
head 160304 Read or write by block number. In: R0 = block, R1 = words (>0 read, <0
head 160304 write), R2 = address, R3 = the driver's work area, UNIT = drive. Out: C
head 160304 set on an error, its code in ERRFDD (52).

code 160422 SUBRW
head 160422 Read or write by sector. In the work area: ADDR = address, WCNT = words
head 160422 (>0 read, <0 write), SIDE (0 lower, 1 upper), TRK = track, UNIT = drive,
head 160422 SECTOR.

code 160566 READ
head 160566 Read an array: start the motor and note the drive.

code 160572 MAIN
head 160572 The main part of reading or writing an array: seek the track, then work
head 160572 sector by sector.

code 160720 ERR12
head 160720 Leave with error 12 (the sectors are the wrong length).

code 160724 ERR
head 160724 Leave with an error.

code 160730 QUIT
head 160730 Leave normally.

code 160734 WORK
head 160734 The read itself.

code 161344 NEXT
head 161344 Multi-sector operations: one sector done, take it off the length.

code 161466 VECT4
head 161466 Bus error (vector 4) during a disk operation.

code 161474 ERROR
head 161474 Leave with the error code (stored in ERRFDD).

code 161510 EXIT
head 161510 Leave without an error (C cleared in the saved PSW).

code 161514 EXIT1
head 161514 Restore vector 4 and return.

code 161542 TSTCRC
head 161542 Check the CRC.

code 161564 RDSEC
head 161564 Read a sector into the buffer; R1 = words to move.

code 161634 FINDS
head 161634 Find the sync sequence.

code 161706 STREAD
head 161706 Start reading.

code 161732 FINDH
head 161732 Find an address marker.

code 162106 INDEX
head 162106 Check that a disk is in and count its revolutions (the index pulse).

code 162224 ENGINE
head 162224 Select the drive and start its motor.

name 162374 DMASK
head 162374 Masks that switch the drives on.

code 162400 SETPTR
head 162400 Set the FLGPTR pointer to the drive's flag byte.

code 162434 GOTRK
head 162434 Seek to the track.

code 162512 GOUP
head 162512 Step the head in (towards the centre): the track number goes up by 1.

code 162536 GODOWN
head 162536 Step the head out: the track number goes down by 1.

code 162562 STEPHD
head 162562 One head step, with its delay. (STEP in the source.)

code 162634 GOTO00
head 162634 Go back to track 0.

code 162700 FRESEC
head 162700 Skip a sector.

code 162704 FICT
head 162704 Skip R0 words of data.

code 162762 WRSEC
head 162762 Write a sector; R1 = words to write.

code 163074 WRMAR
head 163074 Write a data marker, after R0 words of 4E4E.

code 163166 CORR
head 163166 Set the write precompensation.

code 163220 FORMAT
head 163220 Format a track.
